Subject: [PATCH] venus: preserve DRM identity for wlroots renderers

Venus hides DRM and PCI identity on NVIDIA to force WSI clients onto the
prime blit path. This also prevents wlroots' Vulkan renderer from matching
its DRM device, causing Aqueous startup to fail with VulkanRendererUnavailable.

Like Gamescope, the wlroots Vulkan renderer does not use WSI swapchains.
Preserve its guest device identity when the engine is wlroots and
VK_KHR_surface is not enabled. Keep the existing workaround for WSI clients,
including any wlroots instance that enables VK_KHR_surface.

Based on Mesa 26.2.4.

diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_wsi.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_wsi.c
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_wsi.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_wsi.c
@@ -148,14 +148,20 @@
     *    late to reject LINEAR mod when the native image path has already
     *    been taken instead of the prime image path.
     *
-    * Gamescope requires VK_EXT_physical_device_drm and its runtime doesn't
-    * use standard WSI extensions, so venus can spoof without impacting it.
+    * Gamescope and the wlroots Vulkan renderer require
+    * VK_EXT_physical_device_drm to match the guest DRM device. Neither uses
+    * standard WSI extensions for rendering. Keep the wlroots exception limited
+    * to instances without VK_KHR_surface so WSI clients retain the workaround.
     */
    struct vk_properties *props = &physical_dev->base.vk.properties;
    const bool is_nvidia = props->vendorID == 0x10de;
    const char *app_name = physical_dev->instance->base.vk.app_info.app_name;
    const bool is_gamescope = app_name && strcmp(app_name, "gamescope") == 0;
-   if (is_nvidia && !is_gamescope) {
+   const char *engine_name = physical_dev->instance->base.vk.app_info.engine_name;
+   const bool is_wlroots_renderer =
+      engine_name && strcmp(engine_name, "wlroots") == 0 &&
+      !physical_dev->instance->base.vk.enabled_extensions.KHR_surface;
+   if (is_nvidia && !is_gamescope && !is_wlroots_renderer) {
       /* Fail same_gpu check on x11. See wsi_device_matches_drm_fd. */
       physical_dev->base.vk.supported_extensions.EXT_pci_bus_info = false;
       props->pciDomain = 0;
